    docs: correct the portable hint-table coverage claims for this fork
    
    The hint tables' five measured CI runs are upstream's, and they cover the
    lane sizes upstream held when they ran. This fork's serial lane carries
    additional fork-only members no upstream run measured, so state that they
    pack on the PORTABLE_SERIAL_DEFAULT_WEIGHT_MS default until the fork
    refreshes its own hints, and point at bin/fm-test-run.sh --check-coverage
    for the live lane size and unmeasured share instead of a count copied here.
    Generalize the refresh command's -R owner placeholder to match.

